<section class="about-section wrap" id="about"><div><p class="eyebrow lcd">The personal bit</p><h2>Why these<br>projects.</h2></div><div class="about-copy"><p>I wanted to make simple puzzle and arcade games my two daughters could play on their tablets or my retro handhelds. I spend more time tinkering with the handhelds than playing games on them, so it’s nice when the kids get to enjoy the games.</p><p>After seeing tablet games ask for money as soon as my daughters finish the first level, I made them a candy-themed kart racer. That held their attention for a day, which is a high compliment, I think. Next up might be another game they like—or something to help my six-year-old with reading.</p><dl><div><dt>Based in</dt><dd>Mississauga, Ontario</dd></div><div><dt>Makes</dt><dd>Games &amp; tools</dd></div><div><dt>What's next?</dt><dd>A nap</dd></div></dl></div></section>

